    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nexrc comes very handy per my usecases, but sometimes i need to ignore exrc and just run the editor. one case would be using `nvim` as my git commit message editor in the folder with exrc. \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI can run `--no-exrc` or similar flag, so my configuration applies, but project-specific settings do not",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "How would this differ from `nvim --cmd 'set noexrc'` ? Generally I think we should avoid new `--foo` options because they are redundant with the editor mechanisms.\n\nIf you are setting 'exrc' in your config, you can make it conditional by checking `nvim_get_option_info2()` to see if it was set by `--cmd` (I think). There might be a better way too.",
            "created_at": "2026-11-02T11:24:48Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42651#issuecomment-6575933585",
