        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> If you are setting 'exrc' in your config, you can make it conditional by checking nvim_get_option_info2() to see if it was set by --cmd (I think). There might be a better way too.\n\nYep, I am setting it there and that's why it is invoked in the first place. Setting it with --cmd takes no effect, because --cmd runs before my config as far as I understand that.\n\n---\n\n```lua\nif not vim.api.nvim_get_option_info2('exrc').was_set then\n    vim.opt.exrc = true\nend\n```\n\nwith `export VISUAL=\"nvim --cmd 'set noexrc'\"`\n\nJust checked, this works fine, I imagined that flag being pretty standard, but if you think it's pretty exotic usecase, then I think the issue might be closed. Thanks for such quick reply.",
